# runtime state anywhere in the tree (not source) — nested .omc/.evor
**/.omc/
# ── P-02 / Q-01: the installed plugin must ship NO run state ────────────────
#
# The repo tracked `.evor/active-run.json` and a whole
# `.evor/runs/frontier-1ms/run-live-01/` tree — a CIFAR-10 self-test mission —
# so every install carried a fake ACTIVE RUN inside the plugin root. That is the
# decoy Q-01's hooks resolved to for 19 hours: they were not finding stale state
# left by the user's own run, they were finding state the package shipped.
#
# 1.3 stopped the hooks resolving there, 6.x stopped the MCP server writing
# there, and P-02 stopped the harness writing there. This stops it being SHIPPED,
# which is the only one of the four that removes the thing rather than avoiding it.
#
# Anchored (`/.evor/`) and unanchored (`**/.evor/`) both: `mcp/.evor/` had a
# tracked `signals-inbox.jsonl` too.
/.evor/
**/.evor/
.evor/runs/
.evor/active-run.json

# generated CI evidence artifacts
ci/out/

logs/

# Local benchmark mission scratch (see ci/bench-tick.sh — normally runs in-container)
.evor-bench/

# machine-local Claude Code overrides
.claude/settings.local.json
